": "concept", "title": "Covenant Code"}, {"id": "61cf9f76-6b6b-4e19-aeff-d428bbd9e927", "type": "concept", "title": "Law and narrative"}], "description": "Students learn to read biblical law as social and theological instruction rather than a modern legal code alone."}, {"id": "e3786708-e1e6-497a-ab6c-a32a11410885", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ritual and holiness", "children": [{"id": "564fffa9-cdd8-4c32-baa8-b4eee55dbdcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Sacrifice"}, {"id": "45649144-11f7-4d79-adf2-bfe9604b588e", "type": "concept", "title": "Purity and impurity"}, {"id": "0cd1a7ae-482c-4ea5-835e-b850328e9026", "type": "concept", "title": "Holy time and sacred space"}], "description": "Priestly texts teach students how ritual, body, space, and time organize sacred life."}, {"id": "ee4609aa-c235-4f44-825f-035d7c9b0021", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethics and social life", "children": [{"id": "c498486b-785b-4151-8890-2f8e775423c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Stranger, widow, and orphan"}, {"id": "4aeb496e-10bf-442f-9881-67d3403ddf35", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt and land"}, {"id": "502ff61f-0952-43b3-b215-b2eb494ef4b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Sex, food, and identity"}], "description": "The course asks how law imagines community, justice, care, and boundaries."}]}, {"id": "4f763a16-f16e-4da5-837c-772eae16ec56", "type": "topic", "title": "Deuteronomy, Covenant Renewal, Land, and the Deuteronomistic History", "description": "Connects Deuteronomy's covenant theology to Joshua, Judges, Samuel, and Kings.", "children": [{"id": "f776f688-dc93-4dbb-87a8-8ffd051d469e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deuteronomy's voice", "children": [{"id": "32a72e64-c594-4a44-bc63-e6b6eccec726", "type": "concept", "title": "Moses' speeches"}, {"id": "75962ab6-e44e-423d-a10f-c7f4b53cb3f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Centralization of worship"}, {"id": "3cd952bc-32bd-493c-970f-908ed0557f02", "type": "concept", "title": "Blessing and curse"}], "description": "Students examine Deuteronomy as a retelling and reinterpretation of law, memory, and covenant."}, {"id": "e2e325da-a27d-419d-b555-849125959fc3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Land and obedience", "children": [{"id": "bf35c3c6-6a11-49d8-acac-557d050647da", "type": "concept", "title": "Conquest language"}, {"id": "11857929-d9cd-4154-8542-1bef6cf720fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Covenant loyalty"}, {"id": "11a835bf-4d80-45c7-aa69-20efc03e8f9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Memory and warning"}], "description": "The course explores how land becomes theological promise and ethical responsibility."}, {"id": "523198e8-dc36-492f-88d6-e95f3aa6f98d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deuteronomistic history", "children": [{"id": "8a773f71-dd0c-45ea-a676-5b86e259cd42", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycles of faithfulness and failure"}, {"id": "4c252412-d370-42c9-a4db-c79e01de119f", "type": "concept", "title": "Leadership evaluation"}, {"id": "420971cb-d111-4ee8-820a-b5189765e1ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Exile as interpretation"}], "description": "Students connect Deuteronomy's themes to Joshua, Judges, Samuel, and Kings."}]}, {"id": "3b580250-6372-43bf-a7bf-f08793fa3587", "type": "topic", "title": "Conquest, Judges, Monarchy, Temple, and Divided Kingdoms", "description": "Follows Israel and Judah through settlement traditions, charismatic leadership, kingship, temple ideology, and political crisis.", "children": [{"id": "f83987ab-1044-44a4-9cba-eb5cae5b4097", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Joshua and Judges", "children": [{"id": "7b1adb4a-5ed8-42a4-855a-19960ffd978c", "type": "concept", "title": "Jericho and Ai"}, {"id": "9430aa1e-2820-4f44-a245-8c4192ce4da1", "type": "concept", "title": "Tribal confederacy"}, {"id": "dd09b74c-bb89-429a-aa20-7faf788f0bdb", "type": "concept", "title": "Violence and memory"}], "description": "Students analyze settlement traditions and the difficult ethical questions raised by conquest narratives."}, {"id": "2e832e4b-7149-455d-8c07-994b5b795d22", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monarchy and kingship", "children": [{"id": "f3873155-3029-43ca-a4ea-f7ebffd97e22", "type": "concept", "title": "Saul, David, and Solomon"}, {"id": "5b54f434-1678-42ff-aa4b-00b91a5d85fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Dynasty and succession"}, {"id": "5d23da4c-41c2-491d-9c88-3922a77180ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Royal ideology"}], "description": "The monarchy narratives debate power, charisma, legitimacy, and failure."}, {"id": "9d9faa91-e614-4016-984c-b9b53848b5dc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Temple and kingdoms", "children": [{"id": "98037217-c42c-485a-af63-e53bc4926518", "type": "concept", "title": "Jerusalem temple"}, {"id": "cdd2b25e-3cac-4213-a9ae-f9c335cdf7b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Israel and Judah"}, {"id": "f3d076c6-2ccd-4c22-9462-b0f1c7b994f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Assyrian and Babylonian crises"}], "description": "Students follow the divided kingdoms through worship, politics, prophetic critique, and imperial pressure."}]}, {"id": "6c0d1be1-e89b-4d6a-92ea-bb249b050e56", "type": "topic", "title": "Prophecy, Social Critique, Empire, and Hope", "description": "Studies prophets as poets, critics, theologians, and political interpreters of crisis and possibility.", "children": [{"id": "dbea32cd-03de-4e0a-8092-1e6df67c21ce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prophetic vocation", "children": [{"id": "881b0d80-3af2-4e80-86be-47afa8197e32", "type": "concept", "title": "Call narratives"}, {"id": "e502d6fe-df29-4733-8755-65c5afeaa126", "type": "concept", "title": "Symbolic actions"}, {"id": "d747bb60-88f6-4bde-9fc6-616c33d047e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Oracles and disputation"}], "description": "Students learn prophecy as interpretation of public life rather than simply prediction of the future."}, {"id": "ce3715ba-d123-43d5-ac47-b5195fb53bcb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Justice and critique", "children": [{"id": "5e377062-4478-4203-860f-c53be8920ecb", "type": "concept", "title": "Amos and exploitation"}, {"id": "6bc7bded-2bc4-4bb6-9a52-72010bd7733a", "type": "concept", "title": "Isaiah and holiness"}, {"id": "d31f8f67-4f57-4232-80cb-a9fd591189fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Micah and justice"}], "description": "The prophets connect worship, economics, violence, and social responsibility."}, {"id": "c95fc4e5-8744-416c-8ab8-817c595b427d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Judgment and hope", "children": [{"id": "2906e834-c680-4d27-93a4-e68ea5add4df", "type": "concept", "title": "Day of the Lord"}, {"id": "7f4dea89-14e0-4096-b1a7-6087a7754625", "type": "concept", "title": "Remnant themes"}, {"id": "0c7b5618-3aad-46c2-8a98-cef1b5b8d706", "type": "concept", "title": "New covenant and restoration"}], "description": "Students examine how prophetic books hold catastrophe and restoration together."}]}, {"id": "a70099e0-73f2-403f-b927-2cabe40aa151", "type": "topic", "title": "Psalms, Lament, Worship, and Biblical Poetry", "description": "Reads psalms and poetic texts as practices of praise, protest, memory, ritual, and public theology.", "children": [{"id": "67000452-dbdc-4603-8fb5-c3d8e313c0b2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Poetic form", "children": [{"id": "904e0789-ba7c-4b52-a96c-9af289a595f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Parallelism"}, {"id": "55ee85c3-492d-4659-b937-e54eed15d6d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Imagery and metaphor"}, {"id": "f8735de1-6a78-41e5-ad35-c9e67ddfc4b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Acrostic and structure"}], "description": "Students learn the mechanics of Hebrew poetry so they can interpret the texts with care."}, {"id": "78e35e4b-6bdd-4644-912a-04594bb26a81", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Psalms as prayer", "children": [{"id": "928857fb-88f3-46bf-b3bb-8b3e8eb5f702", "type": "concept", "title": "Praise and thanksgiving"}, {"id": "611386dc-d636-472a-ad03-024b8fc2fa62", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual and communal lament"}, {"id": "6e820eb1-122a-4f9e-8070-7f07df54bae8", "type": "concept", "title": "Royal and wisdom psalms"}], "description": "The Psalms teach speech to God in praise, grief, anger, trust, and communal ritual."}, {"id": "9815f450-576d-4f8f-8685-77cba8e4ddbd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lament and trauma", "children": [{"id": "499b4179-8b37-46b0-a052-0e4053ea0dee", "type": "concept", "title": "Lamentations"}, {"id": "96f881a3-3ae8-498b-a796-6d33e5c13867", "type": "concept", "title": "Complaint and accusation"}, {"id": "f9a6b034-2168-4e45-aa02-4a1550843931", "type": "concept", "title": "Public grief"}], "description": "Students study lament as a disciplined language for catastrophe, protest, and memory."}]}, {"id": "f4955aa3-ded3-4fae-a372-51ba0bb9e38f", "type": "topic", "title": "Wisdom Literature: Proverbs, Job, Ecclesiastes, and the Limits of Order", "description": "Explores wisdom as moral instruction, practical counsel, philosophical challenge, and debate about suffering.", "children": [{"id": "ecfa61cf-b2df-4047-b7ff-a32363de0c0e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Proverbs and moral order", "children": [{"id": "c10a79d3-8990-4a9f-af1c-948665709888", "type": "concept", "title": "Short sayings"}, {"id": "d6a2bec0-51cb-4b0e-8e22-0c0c87f7e725", "type": "concept", "title": "Woman Wisdom"}, {"id": "c9638e14-6957-4bc7-8070-4e9014030726", "type": "concept", "title": "Instruction and formation"}], "description": "Students read Proverbs as practical instruction in discipline, speech, labor, family, and social responsibility."}, {"id": "9a76b51e-54c6-4c8d-82ee-093f4b169fd0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Job and suffering", "children": [{"id": "4b08f66a-2ffc-4704-8aff-5bdc8cb04e26", "type": "concept", "title": "Prologue and dialogues"}, {"id": "0b5d1cee-6c06-4052-8959-9e467fb14e83", "type": "concept", "title": "Friends' arguments"}, {"id": "fd6580bc-c6af-4e35-be9d-49a6d8c58255", "type": "concept", "title": "Divine speeches"}], "description": "Job challenges simple moral equations and opens questions about justice, speech, and divine silence."}, {"id": "f02eabcc-0fa2-418d-971d-b4126c47a71f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ecclesiastes and ambiguity", "children": [{"id": "b268a443-b95e-408e-be53-f6529965dd92", "type": "concept", "title": "Vanity and vapor"}, {"id": "fa11282b-3f8d-4b93-b0d9-f52b02ef319d", "type": "concept", "title": "Death and time"}, {"id": "37556d50-9680-40d7-ab3b-85072c403602", "type": "concept", "title": "Joy, limits, and skepticism"}], "description": "Ecclesiastes teaches students how biblical wisdom can question certainty and easy meaning."}]}, {"id": "d11a43d9-b0a0-4c3c-ae93-21ff4f15bea4", "type": "topic", "title": "Exile, Trauma, Return, Restoration, and Scriptural Formation", "description": "Interprets exile and return as historical crisis, theological reckoning, and engine of literary preservation.", "children": [{"id": "4445f390-1cb6-4b75-80f8-76d08c79ee9d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exile as crisis", "children": [{"id": "9cc10ad4-2061-4df7-a24f-2506f05d55e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Fall of Jerusalem"}, {"id": "12c57e57-f213-4c0c-8724-85e8728ecf33", "type": "concept", "title": "Temple destruction"}, {"id": "ee4e1135-91d0-4ffc-a1bd-e0829aee6496", "type": "concept", "title": "Displacement and identity"}], "description": "Students examine exile as political catastrophe, theological problem, and literary turning point."}, {"id": "86f6c73c-aeb7-475e-b5e4-d8ed0a7aa52b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exilic and postexilic voices", "children": [{"id": "c433f44a-351e-45d7-945b-db13eec232f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Jeremiah and Ezekiel"}, {"id": "e59ed97a-07ba-49a0-bb19-f1cd95eeaaba", "type": "concept", "title": "Second Isaiah"}, {"id": "59534a67-3cd2-4d87-9739-aca2bdb67b84", "type": "concept", "title": "Ezra and Nehemiah"}], "description": "The course reads texts that reimagine community after devastation."}, {"id": "95e51644-6300-4b66-ae69-dcca9946ca7c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scriptural formation", "children": [{"id": "203cfee1-8c6a-4c0c-a69e-0b437a8294c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Scribal culture"}, {"id": "d2a212cb-e875-4d23-8