emple-centered memory"}, {"id": "6d950b28-3ea8-4192-a649-fa1e7b50e380", "type": "concept", "title": "Second Temple context"}], "description": "Students learn how later biblical texts retell earlier stories for new communities."}]}, {"id": "00f2140f-41de-4a64-9301-89f779733959", "type": "topic", "title": "Reception, Interpretation, Ethics, and Contemporary Uses of the Hebrew Bible", "description": "Asks how the Hebrew Bible has been interpreted, contested, taught, translated, and used in modern moral and political discourse.", "children": [{"id": "76a93326-6eed-47c7-a702-8bb2232ab77c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jewish and Christian reception", "children": [{"id": "1e283e76-0d4e-494b-9d17-afd8da97994f", "type": "concept", "title": "Rabbinic interpretation"}, {"id": "2d279513-5f6e-4a6c-9b25-721284f4da5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Christian Old Testament readings"}, {"id": "721d4514-48a7-42a3-b79d-061b11103b04", "type": "concept", "title": "Translation and canon differences"}], "description": "Students explore how communities interpret shared texts differently."}, {"id": "31a3b5a9-a757-4ede-ac79-24c614387e1e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical interpretation", "children": [{"id": "3b3c84cf-1ede-4f05-81af-b148f2a50cce", "type": "concept", "title": "Violence and conquest"}, {"id": "e4a1d919-738a-49f0-86c1-1bc987486301", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender and power"}, {"id": "12da6c5b-d9e4-43ec-a4c8-5aa6a0e15446", "type": "concept", "title": "Slavery, law, and moral change"}], "description": "The course asks how to read difficult texts responsibly in modern classrooms and public life."}, {"id": "c5b35df7-6da9-4224-aa39-de75cab86b00", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modern cultural afterlives", "children": [{"id": "a8999fd2-d45d-4d78-8692-1e2f4a721add", "type": "concept", "title": "Literature and visual art"}, {"id": "5fb5c0bf-5b91-4315-95fe-c654860e14c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Public rhetoric"}, {"id": "ad7f9911-9d63-4564-8f31-cbdf30e8ff5a", "type": "conc