 {"id": "8484b02a-7501-4030-ab16-cc0b64b9de46", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparison of translations"}], "description": "Students learn to slow down and ask literary, historical, and interpretive questions of primary texts."}]}, {"id": "bcebe7fa-aea9-416d-a456-a74079abc79b", "type": "topic", "title": "Canon, Textual History, Manuscripts, and Translation", "description": "Introduces Tanakh, Hebrew Bible, Old Testament, textual witnesses, and the stakes of translation.", "children": [{"id": "cfc7cce5-8a37-4df2-a263-c3c0576df821", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Canon formation", "children": [{"id": "080a9488-773e-4940-a39d-08bd0b349e3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Torah, Prophets, Writings"}, {"id": "ff0c4389-138a-4ed9-bcbd-b2b2deac08c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Canon boundaries"}, {"id": "6154ae9c-c8a9-46b7-a566-b87a42b1053b", "type": "concept", "title": "Book order and theology"}], "description": "Students examine how collections become authoritative and how order shapes interpretation."}, {"id": "d1ba8fb6-bc17-4770-abdf-a86612e60d35", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Textual witnesses", "children": [{"id": "767ef59c-e186-4581-9b13-6e50c8de76ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Masoretic Text"}, {"id": "f254e976-3e8a-4b36-8106-f14c9ec31261", "type": "concept", "title": "Dead Sea Scrolls"}, {"id": "a498c123-06b4-41dd-9a25-59ed0c488992", "type": "concept", "title": "Septuagint and Samaritan Pentateuch"}], "description": "The gist is that the Hebrew Bible has a textual history, not just a single timeless form."}, {"id": "c551c769-5bb1-468b-af66-043dc39fdec8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Translation choices", "children": [{"id": "cb4acf0b-e32f-4415-99a9-78a9cc48f4c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Formal and dynamic translation"}, {"id": "2461981b-5bc0-4160-9616-07f61474affa", "type": "concept", "title": "Key Hebrew terms"}, {"id": "daa2b3a1-342a-483f-908e-8e9f613ce9ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Footnotes and textual variants"}], "description": "Students learn that translations are interpretations that shape theology, tone, and meaning."}]}, {"id": "bcf0fa0b-bc4a-4a6c-b5c1-8135666e0436", "type": "topic", "title": "Ancient Near Eastern Context, Geography, Archaeology, and History", "description": "Places biblical literature in the worlds of Egypt, Mesopotamia, Canaan, Israel, Judah, empire, land, and material culture.", "children": [{"id": "26d7d3c7-6e20-4f1b-ad34-d5cbc23a747a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regional worlds", "children": [{"id": "9bc2b06b-228a-4b6b-a4c1-dd2b1f5dcfe2", "type": "concept", "title": "Egypt and Mesopotamia"}, {"id": "1c32c4c5-3b65-4631-8490-c7fd4d8c5c1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Canaan and the Levant"}, {"id": "142a5c63-a5d5-4404-8d41-5bf9c5eda4e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Assyria, Babylon, and Persia"}], "description": "Students place Israel and Judah within the wider eastern Mediterranean and Near Eastern environment."}, {"id": "6e64e63b-5347-4ab5-b739-507e2fc96f7c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Land and geography", "children": [{"id": "eaaac06e-10a6-47c2-9b6a-9e087b7a9558", "type": "concept", "title": "Wilderness, highlands, coast, and valleys"}, {"id": "46e71b9c-1def-461f-8def-b8af10d07314", "type": "concept", "title": "Jerusalem and temple geography"}, {"id": "26debfd6-3833-421a-b434-6478d6b541c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Borders and imagined land"}], "description": "The course links narrative, law, prophecy, and poetry to place."}, {"id": "8788d025-9ab0-4fdf-a72d-b5ad63655092", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Archaeology and evidence", "children": [{"id": "4a240bf4-6d52-4db5-9ed0-f18d9503af8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Inscriptions and seals"}, {"id": "16df1b37-60be-421b-a15d-b822fd689d30", "type": "concept", "title": "Settlement patterns"}, {"id": "e3de49e2-a681-442b-b960-749707eb1058", "type": "concept", "title": "Limits of archaeological correlation"}], "description": "Students learn what material evidence can and cannot prove about biblical texts."}]}, {"id": "8f9182f3-0d3d-4bf6-9f7a-872c9b711e7b", "type": "topic", "title": "Methods of Interpretation: Historical, Literary, Source, Redaction, and Reception Criticism", "description": "Builds the toolkit students need to read texts critically and compare scholarly arguments.", "children": [{"id": "c4f1c370-c3de-4463-a31d-92d4bcaf6a02", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical-critical methods", "children": [{"id": "170e4759-8b4f-4e90-8f46-bc7efb6c742b", "type": "concept", "title": "Source criticism"}, {"id": "e887a29c-f734-4689-88b6-bd43cc32409d", "type": "concept", "title": "Form and tradition criticism"}, {"id": "39932d01-196f-408c-a3c0-f955587f0a94", "type": "concept", "title": "Redaction criticism"}], "description": "Students learn why scholars ask about sources, authorship, dating, editing, and historical setting."}, {"id": "42c15f12-5e4a-4cab-bbbe-e9b412b1f7e5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Literary methods", "children": [{"id": "1ea84b63-80da-4f92-912a-ca379a23d657", "type": "concept", "title": "Plot and characterization"}, {"id": "6cb1a8bd-d420-4fbb-8a2e-86d409910fa5", "type": "concept", "title": "Repetition and type-scenes"}, {"id": "59b59935-2094-4184-bd2c-2da60d6cb978", "type": "concept", "title": "Poetic parallelism"}], "description": "The point is to read biblical texts as crafted narratives and poems with structure, voice, and ambiguity."}, {"id": "f7cf84fe-0d3a-43a1-a5b3-f445274f97dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reception and critical approaches", "children": [{"id": "e2e807fd-4ce9-42f8-816e-75a1dca281be", "type": "concept", "title": "Feminist and gender criticism"}, {"id": "16b419a0-6502-4705-8804-f65fb4bd73ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Postcolonial critique"}, {"id": "ab3112ee-40ad-4803-b42c-5d6bad72412d", "type": "concept", "title": "Jewish, Christian, and secular reception"}], "description": "Students see how texts generate later interpretations and how modern questions reshape readings."}]}, {"id": "fc7532b3-082e-4aee-abaa-a38949756f7d", "type": "topic", "title": "Creation, Primeval History, Myth, Genealogy, and Human Origins", "description": "Reads Genesis 1-11 as theological, literary, and cultural reflection on creation, violence, kinship, and human limits.", "children": [{"id": "ab8875de-3dc4-4586-8b28-de82a14017bf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genesis creation accounts", "children": [{"id": "55484922-9afb-4595-9ed0-e3267c604b50", "type": "concept", "title": "Genesis 1 and Genesis 2-3"}, {"id": "2203651d-3803-40c6-8726-02122101e81e", "type": "concept", "title": "Image of God"}, {"id": "6bf5cef1-468f-4a37-8947-714b797799ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Sabbath and creation order"}], "description": "Students compare creation traditions as theological and literary claims about order, humanity, and God."}, {"id": "ef96b8e4-3d42-48b4-af5c-d1f9967e12bf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Primeval narratives", "children": [{"id": "506c09e3-896b-4b04-9ff4-47e06bfc7188", "type": "concept", "title": "Cain and Abel"}, {"id": "028c1a01-6d85-4644-9271-acf8967b2d6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Flood traditions"}, {"id": "880e328a-1c23-40ff-9025-1ec92207a493", "type": "concept", "title": "Tower of Babel"}], "description": "The course reads early Genesis as reflection on violence, limits, and divine-human relations."}, {"id": "f6891fff-baf5-4cb0-8469-fe238a0d81d0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Myth and genealogy", "children": [{"id": "98ab9a72-d503-4592-a2e7-2f1b9a821783", "type": "concept", "title": "Ancient Near Eastern parallels"}, {"id": "779332bf-df53-44eb-9b5d-b1b5ba26d863", "type": "concept", "title": "Genealogies and identity"}, {"id": "e8893470-82a7-4f31-b728-5ccdf7619148", "type": "concept", "title": "Etiology and cultural memory"}], "description": "Students learn to use 'myth' analytically rather than dismissively."}]}, {"id": "cf74e878-7555-4510-875e-965485f3b605", "type": "topic", "title": "Ancestors, Matriarchs and Patriarchs, Covenant, Promise, and Identity", "description": "Studies Genesis 12-50 as family narrative, migration story, covenant tradition, and identity formation.", "children": [{"id": "349b14ad-4da8-4f8f-8d43-7f747c1b86ed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Call and promise", "children": [{"id": "51464fc8-8d4c-4fdb-8ea1-6277a8b13915", "type": "concept", "title": "Genesis 12"}, {"id": "6579fbdb-8d22-4fd1-b0d9-0777deb9ab3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Promise and delay"}, {"id": "b6e6147e-687c-47aa-8237-070f38a630ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Covenant signs"}], "description": "Students examine Abraham and Sarah traditions as narratives of migration, land, descendants, and blessing."}, {"id": "ee8abadd-0c71-4fb1-9b32-56989ce57bd8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Family conflict and identity", "children": [{"id": "b9752328-cda5-474e-8d8e-1c0d6c6b2d17", "type": "concept", "title": "Hagar and Ishmael"}, {"id": "bf1817bc-13bd-4c72-80cb-75a077e88b37", "type": "concept", "title": "Jacob and Esau"}, {"id": "ff525833-41d8-465d-8270-ad6e0ce8e6e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Joseph and his brothers"}], "description": "The ancestral stories explore kinship, rivalry, gender, inheritance, and survival."}, {"id": "cceaa587-2194-421d-af78-e1b221050813", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Covenant traditions", "children": [{"id": "c63d2f51-59d5-4ab9-9923-96709b7743b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Land and descendants"}, {"id": "c2ddec8e-26fe-4f82-acc3-a9f118b9b530", "type": "concept", "title": "Election and blessing"}, {"id": "31c1637b-58bf-4745-8ae7-3a7ca6d75153", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative tension and divine promise"}], "description": "Students learn how covenant language organizes identity, obligation, and memory."}]}, {"id": "b4691efe-c3f4-4235-afaf-3dda59126a9e", "type": "topic", "title": "Exodus, Liberation, Wilderness, Sinai, and Memory", "description": "Examines Exodus and wilderness traditions as stories of oppression, deliverance, revelation, rebellion, and communal memory.", "children": [{"id": "74eb2f16-f289-429f-be20-6565fcfc81b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Oppression and deliverance", "children": [{"id": "4a1f42f1-f24b-46b8-abe0-daa6ee1133b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Pharaoh and empire"}, {"id": "51d5f028-12b3-4cdd-9675-d0361bc64182", "type": "concept", "title": "Plagues and power"}, {"id": "a3abb9b4-c590-4bc5-a2bb-1ba034bbe4ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Passover memory"}], "description": "Students read Exodus as a foundational memory of slavery, resistance, and divine liberation."}, {"id": "9b0c0ddb-f432-40cd-9f64-50c2f9bac4aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wilderness testing", "children": [{"id": "42981626-4362-45a3-b6d0-a6af1bf765a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Manna and water"}, {"id": "99c2a0a1-aee8-4fee-b60a-894941608445", "type": "concept", "title": "Murmuring traditions"}, {"id": "8fa84731-c398-48f6-bdd8-32efc96ab5c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Moses and mediation"}], "description": "The wilderness traditions explore dependence, fear, leadership, and communal formation."}, {"id": "15d86ede-291a-403b-8be9-307467e86870", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sinai and revelation", "children": [{"id": "53f590f7-87b4-4346-b761-eb0bccd03528", "type": "concept", "title": "Decalogue"}, {"id": "c2d2d08a-f517-4293-b5bf-bfea5bf009b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Covenant ceremony"}, {"id": "aa06fe6a-73e6-47e4-859b-f29ea77321a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Golden calf and intercession"}], "description": "Students study Sinai as a narrative of covenant, law, worship, and identity."}]}, {"id": "d840bc7f-f8fd-4303-860b-0f3924ce10ce", "type": "topic", "title": "Torah Law, Ritual, Holiness, Priestly Thought, and Ethics", "description": "Explores biblical law and ritual as social imagination, theology, practice, and ethical formation.", "children": [{"id": "e4830a8e-ba2a-499c-a933-6746d880a138", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Law as instruction", "children": [{"id": "8e9de537-91d7-4078-9d81-69bbbb5b8138", "type": "concept", "title": "Apodictic and casuistic law"}, {"id": "73e6eeef-3854-44e7-b4d4-5e61b8ff6687", "type": "concept", "title": "Covenant Code"}, {"id": "61cf9f76-6b6b-4e19-aeff-d428bbd9e927", "type": "concept", "title": "Law and narrative"}], "description": "Students learn to read biblical law as social and theological instruction rather than a modern legal code alone."}, {"id": "e3786708-e1e6-497a-ab6c-a32a11410885", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ritual and holiness", "children": [{"id": "564fffa9-cdd8-4c32-baa8-b4eee55dbdcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Sacrifice"}, {"id": "45649144-11f7-4d79-adf2-bfe9604b588e", "type": "concept", "title": "Purity and impurity"}, {"id": "0cd1a7ae-482c-4ea5-835e-b850328e9026", "type": "concept", "title": "Holy time and sacred space"}], "description": "Priestly texts teach students how ritual, body, space, and time organize sacred life."}, {"id": "ee4609aa-c235-4f44-825f-035d7c9b0021", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethics and social life", "children": [{"id": "c498486b-785b-4151-8890-2f8e775423c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Stranger, widow, and orphan"}, {"id": "4aeb496e-10bf-442f-9881-67d3403ddf35", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt and land"}, {"id": "502ff61f-0952-43b3-b215-b2eb494ef4b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Sex, food, and identity"}], "description": "The course asks how law imagines community, justice, care, and boundaries."}]}, {"id": "4f763a16-f16e-4da5-837c-772eae16ec56", "type": "topic", "title": "Deuteronomy, Covenant Renewal, Land, and the Deuteronomistic History", "description": "Connects Deuteronomy's covenant theology to Joshua, Judges, Samuel, and Kings.", "children": [{"id": "f776f688-dc93-4dbb-87a8-8ffd051d469e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deuteronomy's voice", "children": [{"id": "32a72e64-c594-4a44-bc63-e6b6eccec726", "type": "concept", "title": "Moses' speeches"}, {"id": "75962ab6-e44e-423d-a10f-c7f4b53cb3f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Centralization of worship"}, {"id": "3cd952bc-32bd-493c-970f-908ed0557f02", "type": "concept", "title": "Blessing and curse"}], "description": "Students examine Deuteronomy as a retelling and reinterpretation of law, memory, and covenant."}, {"id": "e2e325da-a27d-419d-b555-849125959fc3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Land and obedience", "children": [{"id": "bf35c3c6-6a11-49d8-acac-557d050647da", "type": "concept", "title": "Conquest language"}, {"id": "11857929-d9cd-4154-8542-1bef6cf720fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Covenant loyalty"}, {"id": "11a835bf-4d80-45c7-aa69-20efc03e8f9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Memory and warning"}], "description": "The course explores how land becomes theological promise and ethical responsibility."}, {"id": "523198e8-dc36-492f-88d6-e95f3aa6f98d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deuteronomistic history", "children": [{"id": "8a773f71-dd0c-45ea-a676-5b86e259cd42", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycles of faithfulness and failure"}, {"id": "4c252412-d370-42c9-a4db-c79e01de119f", "type": "concept", "title": "Leadership evaluation"}, {"id": "420971cb-d111-4ee8-820a-b5189765e1ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Exile as interpretation"}], "description": "Students connect Deuteronomy's themes to Joshua, Judges, Samuel, and Kings."}]}, {"id": "3b580250-6372-43bf-a7bf-f08793fa3587", "type": "topic", "title": "Conquest, Judges, Monarchy, Temple, and Divided Kingdoms", "description": "Follows Israel and Judah through settlement traditions, charismatic leadership, kingship, temple ideology, and political crisis.", "children": [{"id": "f83987ab-1044-44a4-9cba-eb5cae5b4097", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Joshua and Judges", "children": [{"id": "7b1adb4a-5ed8-42a4-855a-19960ffd978c", "type": "concept", "title": "Jericho and Ai"}, {"id": "9430aa1e-2820-4f44-a245-8c4192ce4da1", "type": "concept", "title": "Tribal confederacy"}, {"id": "dd09b74c-bb89-429a-aa20-7faf788f0bdb", "type": "concept", "title": "Violence and memory"}], "description": "Students analyze settlement traditions and the difficult ethical questions raised by conquest narratives."}, {"id": "2e832e4b-7149-455d-8c07-994b5b795d22", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monarchy and kingship", "children": [{"id": "f3873155-3029-43ca-a4ea-f7ebffd97e22", "type": "concept", "title": "Saul, David, and Solomon"}, {"id": "5b54f434-1678-42ff-aa4b-00b91a5d85fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Dynasty and succession"}, {"id": "5d23da4c-41c2-491d-9c88-3922a77180ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Royal ideology"}], "description": "The monarchy narratives debate power, charisma, legitimacy, and failure."}, {"id": "9d9faa91-e614-4016-984c-b9b53848b5dc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Temple and kingdoms", "children": [{"id": "98037217-c42c-485a-af63-e53bc4926518", "type": "concept", "title": "Jerusalem temple"}, {"id": "cdd2b25e-3cac-4213-a9ae-f9c335cdf7b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Israel and Judah"}, {"id": "f3d076c6-2ccd-4c22-9462-b0f1c7b994f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Assyrian and Babylonian crises"}], "description": "Students follow the divided kingdoms through worship, politics, prophetic critique, and imperial pressure."}]}, {"id": "6c0d1be1-e89b-4d6a-92ea-bb249b050e56", "type": "topic", "title": "Prophecy, Social Critique, Empire, and Hope", "description": "Studies prophets as poets, critics, theologians, and political interpreters of crisis and possibility.", "children": [{"id": "dbea32cd-03de-4e0a-8092-1e6df67c21ce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prophetic vocation", "children": [{"id": "881b0d80-3af2-4e80-86be-47afa8197e32", "type": "concept", "title": "Call narratives"}, {"id": "e502d6fe-df29-4733-8755-65c5afeaa126", "type": "concept", "title": "Symbolic actions"}, {"id": "d747bb60-88f6-4bde-9fc6-616c33d047e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Oracles and disputation"}], "description": "Students learn prophecy as interpretation of public life rather than simply prediction of the future."}, {"id": "ce3715ba-d123-43d5-ac47-b5195fb53bcb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Justice and critique", "children": [{"id": "5e377062-4478-4203-860f-c53be8920ecb", "type": "concept", "title": "Amos and exploitation"}, {"id": "6bc7bded-2bc4-4bb6-9a52-72010bd7733a", "type": "concept", "title": "Isaiah and holiness"}, {"id": "d31f8f67-4f57-4232-80cb-a9fd591189fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Micah and justice"}], "description": "The prophets connect worship, economics, violence, and social responsibility."}, {"id": "c95fc4e5-8744-416c-8ab8-817c595b427d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Judgment and hope", "children": [{"id": "2906e834-c680-4d27-93a4-e68ea5add4df", "type": "concept", "title": "Day of the Lord"}, {"id": "7f4dea89-14e0-4096-b1a7-6087a7754625", "type": "concept", "title": "Remnant themes"}, {"id": "0c7b5618-3aad-46c2-8a98-cef1b5b8d706", "type": "concept", "title": "New covenant and restoration"}], "description": "Students examine how prophetic books hold catastrophe and restoration together."}]}, {"id": "a70099e0-73f2-403f-b927-2cabe40aa151", "type": "topic", "title": "Psalms, Lament, Worship, and Biblical Poetry", "description": "Reads psalms and poetic texts as practices of praise, protest, memory, ritual, and public theology.", "children": [{"id": "67000452-dbdc-4603-8fb5-c3d8e313c0b2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Poetic form", "children": [{"id": "904e0789-ba7c-4b52-a96c-9af289a595f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Parallelism"}, {"id": "55ee85c3-492d-4659-b937-e54eed15d6d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Imagery and metaphor"}, {"id": "f8735de1-6a78-41e5-ad35-c9e67ddfc4b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Acrostic and structure"}], "description": "Students learn the mechanics of Hebrew poetry so they can interpret the texts with care."}, {"id": "78e35e4b-6bdd-4644-912a-04594bb26a81", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Psalms as prayer", "children": [{"id": "928857fb-88f3-46bf-b3bb-8b3e8eb5f702", "type": "concept", "title": "Praise and thanksgiving"}, {"id": "611386dc-d636-472a-ad03-024b8fc2fa62", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual and communal lament"}, {"id": "6e820eb1-122a-4f9e-8070-7f07df54bae8", "type": "concept", "title": "Royal and wisdom psalms"}], "description": "The Psal